<%- include('../partials/legal-top') %>

<p>
  These Terms and Conditions apply to everyone who uses this website, run by
  <%= trust.name %> ("the Trust", "we", "us"), a <%= trust.legalForm.toLowerCase() %>
  based in <%= trust.location %>. By using the website, creating an account,
  donating, becoming a member, volunteering or sending a request, you agree to
  these terms.
</p>

<h2>1. About the Trust</h2>
<p>
  The Trust is managed by its trustees, <%= trust.trustees.map((t) => `${t.name} (${t.role})`).join(' and ') %>.
  It is an independent body and is not linked to any company, including
  Venturecore Solutions Pvt Ltd, or to any political party. Its work is:
</p>
<ul>
  <% trust.programmes.forEach((p) => { %>
    <li><strong><%= p.title %></strong>: <%= p.area.toLowerCase() %>.</li>
  <% }) %>
</ul>
<p>
  Goals and plans shown on the website (for example the number of trees to be
  planted) are targets, not results already achieved.
</p>

<h2>2. Using the website</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Give true, complete and current information in every form.</li>
  <li>Do not misuse the website, try to break its security, or send false or fake requests.</li>
  <li>If you are under 18, use the website only with a parent or guardian.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Accounts</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Keep your password secret. You are responsible for activity on your account.</li>
  <li>Your donation and membership records are shown in your account only after you confirm your email address.</li>
  <li>Tell us at once if you think someone else has used your account. We may suspend an account used for fraud or misuse.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Donations</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Donations are voluntary gifts to the Trust's charitable work.</li>
  <li>
    Money given for a cause (such as Anand Dham or Green Earth) is used only for
    that cause. Money given "Where Most Needed" is used where the trustees
    decide it is most needed.
  </li>
  <li>
    If you choose a purpose within a cause (such as meals for elders or tree
    plantation), we use the money for that purpose where we can. If that need is
    already met, the trustees use it for another need within the same cause.
  </li>
  <li>
    A preferred seva date (for example, meals at Anand Dham on a birthday or a
    death anniversary) is a request. We try our best to keep the date, and will
    tell you if we have to move it.
  </li>
  <li>
    A dedication ("in memory of", "in honour of") is printed on your receipt as
    you typed it. Please check spelling before paying.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Community Temple:</strong> donations to the temple are kept in a
    separate Temple Fund and used only for the temple. Religious donations are
    generally not eligible for tax exemption under Section 80G.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Monthly giving:</strong> choosing "monthly" means we send you a
    reminder email each month. Nothing is debited automatically. You can stop
    the reminders at any time from My Account.
  </li>
  <li>
    <% if (trust.eightyG.approved) { %>
      <strong>Tax receipts:</strong> the Trust is approved under Section 80G
      (Registration No. <%= trust.eightyG.registrationNumber %>, valid
      <%= trust.eightyG.validFrom %> to <%= trust.eightyG.validTo %>). Receipts for
      charitable causes are 80G receipts; Temple Fund gifts are generally not eligible.
    <% } else { %>
      <strong>Tax receipts:</strong> the Trust does not yet have 80G approval.
      Receipts issued now are not 80G receipts and no tax benefit is promised.
      80G receipts will be issued only after approval from the Income Tax Department.
    <% } %>
  </li>
  <li>
    The Trust does not accept foreign contributions, because it does not have
    FCRA registration.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Membership</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Membership is a contribution to support the Trust's work. You receive a membership certificate by email.</li>
  <li>Membership does not give any ownership, voting or management rights in the Trust, and does not make you a trustee.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Payments</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    Payments are processed by PayU, a third-party payment gateway. The Trust
    does not see or store your card, UPI PIN or net banking details.
  </li>
  <li>Refunds are handled under our <a href="/refund-policy">Refund Policy</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Help from the Trust</h2>
<p>
  This covers medical help requests, admission to Anand Dham, Kanyadaan
  support and help under Vidya and Poshan.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>Sending a request does not guarantee help. Each request is checked, and the trustees decide based on need and the funds available.</li>
  <li>We may visit, call, or ask for documents (such as identity proof, income details or hospital papers) before deciding.</li>
  <li>Anand Dham is for senior citizens who are abandoned or have no means of support. Admission depends on a check of the person's situation and on space.</li>
  <li>Kanyadaan support is given only for marriages where both bride and groom are of legal age (18 and 21). The Trust does not support dowry in any form.</li>
  <li>The Trust does not give medical advice. Always follow your doctor's advice.</li>
  <li>Giving false information can lead to a request being rejected, and help already given may be stopped.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Volunteers and events</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Volunteering is unpaid and voluntary. Signing up does not create a job or contract.</li>
  <li>
    At plantation drives, clean-ups, camps and other events, follow the
    instructions of the Trust's coordinator. You take part at your own risk;
    the Trust is not liable for injury or loss of belongings, except where
    caused by its own negligence.
  </li>
  <li>Volunteers under 18 need a parent or guardian's permission.</li>
  <li>Volunteers must treat elders, children and beneficiaries with respect, and must not share their photos or personal details without the Trust's permission.</li>
</ul>

<h2>9. Photos and content</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    The text, logo and images on this website belong to the Trust or are used
    with permission. You may share them for non-commercial purposes with credit
    to the Trust.
  </li>
  <li>
    We take photos at our work and events to report to donors. We publish photos
    of beneficiaries only with their consent (or a guardian's, for children), and
    we do not show the faces of children or elders where they or their families
    ask us not to.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>10. Communication</h2>
<p>
  We contact you by email, phone or WhatsApp only about your donation,
  membership, request or registration. You can ask us to stop at any time.
</p>

<h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
<p>
  The website is provided "as is". The Trust is not liable for indirect loss
  from using the website, for delays or failures of third-party services such
  as the payment gateway, email or WhatsApp, or for events outside its control.
</p>

<h2>12. Changes</h2>
<p>
  We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version.
  Using the website after a change means you accept the updated terms.
</p>

<h2>13. Governing law</h2>
<p>
  These terms are governed by the laws of India. Courts in Basti, Uttar Pradesh
  have jurisdiction over any dispute.
</p>

